¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»For the land, whither thou goest in to possess it, is not as the land of Egypt, from whence ye came out, where thou sowedst thy seed, and wateredst it with thy foot, as a garden of herbs:¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtbut the land, whither ye go to possess it, is a land of hills and valleys, and drinketh water of the rain of heaven:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜a land which the LORD thy God careth for: the eyes of the LORD thy God are always upon it, from the beginning of the year even unto the end of the year.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄAnd it shall come to pass, if ye shall hearken diligently unto my commandments which I command you this day, to love the LORD your God, and to serve him with all your heart and with all your soul,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£that I will give you the rain of your land in his due season, the first rain and the latter rain, that thou mayest gather in thy corn, and thy wine, and thine oil.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd I will send grass in thy fields for thy cattle, that thou mayest eat and be full.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtTake heed to yourselves, that your heart be not deceived, and ye turn aside, and serve other gods, and worship them;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ×and then the LORD's wrath be kindled against you, and he shut up the heaven, that there be no rain, and that the land yield not her fruit; and lest ye perish quickly from off the good land which the LORD giveth you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢Therefore shall ye lay up these my words in your heart and in your soul, and bind them for a sign upon your hand, that they may be as frontlets between your eyes.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªAnd ye shall teach them your children, speaking of them when thou sittest in thine house, and when thou walkest by the way, when thou liest down, and when thou risest up.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQAnd thou shalt write them upon the door posts of thine house, and upon thy gates:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§that your days may be multiplied, and the days of your children, in the land which the LORD sware unto your fathers to give them, as the days of heaven upon the earth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£For if ye shall diligently keep all these commandments which I command you, to do them, to love the LORD your God, to walk in all his ways, and to cleave unto him;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚then will the LORD drive out all these nations from before you, and ye shall possess greater nations and mightier than yourselves.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾Every place whereon the soles of your feet shall tread shall be your's: from the wilderness and Lebanon, from the river, the river Euphrates, even unto the uttermost sea shall your coast be.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙºThere shall no man be able to stand before you: for the LORD your God shall lay the fear of you and the dread of you upon all the land that ye shall tread upon, as he hath said unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9Behold, I set before you this day a blessing and a curse;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[a blessing, if ye obey the commandments of the LORD your God, which I command you this day:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´and a curse, if ye will not obey the commandments of the LORD your God, but turn aside out of the way which I command you this day, to go after other gods, which ye have not known.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉAnd it shall come to pass, when the LORD thy God hath brought thee in unto the land whither thou goest to possess it, that thou shalt put the blessing upon mount Gerizim, and the curse upon mount Ebal.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸Are they not on the other side Jordan, by the way where the sun goeth down, in the land of the Canaanites, which dwell in the champaign over against Gilgal, beside the plains of Moreh?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠFor ye shall pass over Jordan to go in to possess the land which the LORD your God giveth you, and ye shall possess it, and dwell therein.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZAnd ye shall observe to do all the statutes and judgments which I set before you this day.¦layout ªlast_verse 